  "description": "Headless scientific visualization: safely executes OmnibusCloud ParaView packages (a saved .pvsm state plus content-addressed data attachments) and distributes independent rendering tasks across worker nodes. ParaView.Validate treats the state as untrusted input (hardened XML parsing, proxy allowlist, programmable-pipeline rejection, logical-path and plugin-requirement checks, size and resolution limits); ParaView.Split produces deterministic tasks per timestep, each carrying only the attachments its timestep needs (per-task attachment subsetting); ParaView.RenderFrame materializes a task's subset into an isolated package root and renders one output through the controller-owned pvpython runner on the software-rendering baseline; ParaView.Collect returns the ordered frame set. ParaView.Compose (0.3.0) composes a scene from bare data — one blob-referenced CalculiX .frd result plus colouring, colour map, representation and camera choices — on one node into a real saved state, so a result already in the cloud renders with no client-side packaging (RenderParaViewDataStill/Frames/Video). The ParaView runtime ships as per-platform Tier-2 assets, never inside the package.",
